{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} (6'\"\\\\.5|9)|comprehension|cold.error|interactive' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && cat docs/agents/roles/engineer.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} (6'\"\\\\.5|9)|comprehension|cold.error|interactive' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && cat docs/agents/roles/engineer.md\"","aggregated_output":"14:- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems into a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by `dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint interrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel expansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\n15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n139:| **Tier 2: Guest Algebraic Effects** | `yrt.effect` over `%capture` + task-local handler stack (100% guest UAST) | **Any holds:** (1) language-specific or swappable policy (`OverflowError` vs. `Infinity` vs. PHP int64 demotion, test replay); (2) non-local control flow (exceptions, `finally`, PHP `abandon-to`, resumable `yield`); (3) cold/error path; (4) must invoke guest closures. **Zero Jolt kernel cost.** | `raise`/`try`/`finally`, `call-ec`, `abandon-to`, resumable `yield` generators, cold traps (`:math/div-zero`, `:math/overflow`, `:int/bit-limit`, `:int/digit-limit`, `:coll/unsupported-key`), `:runtime/interrupt`. |\n368:  :expr/comprehensions  :supported     ;; eager list/set/dict only; genexpr gated by :control/generators\n403:  ;; Collections, indexing, and comprehension accumulators\n483:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n640:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n678:   - Settled on: (1) `:pure` host value core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, boxed `yin.vm.float`, `kind/namespace`) for total, representation-sensitive ops; (2) unified guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`) for control flow, generators, and cold error/limit policy traps; (3) minimal VM/stream effects (`cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004.\ncat: docs/agents/roles/engineer.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc && sed -n '1,230p' src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc && cat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/contract.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.python.antlr.repl\n  \"The Python ANTLR frontend's REPL lowering (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   section 8.5.6, slice F3). Portable: every host parses with its own\n   generated target of the grammar and lowers the CST packet here.\n\n   One REPL submission lowers to a program that runs the packet's module body\n   against the session's `__main__` namespace: the module object and its\n   globals dict live in `sys.modules` (ruling 18), so a name bound by one\n   submission is read by the next. `(reset)` rebuilds the VM, and with it the\n   runtime state.\n\n   The bundled prelude defines the runtime in the VM's store and `py/init!`\n   allocates its task state; running it twice would discard that state. The\n   first lowering of a session therefore carries the prelude and returns the\n   session marker `:primed`; later lowerings of the same session omit it. The\n   shell keeps the marker (`:frontend-session`) and clears it with the VM.\n\n   The evaluation's value is the last top-level bare expression statement the\n   submission ran (`py/result!`, None when none ran); the REPL loop prints it\n   through the binding's `display-value` (repr, None shows nothing), as it\n   prints any frontend's value. An assignment alone has no value.\n\n   Printed lines and an uncaught exception are rendered by the host\n   primitive `py-report` (`report`) and written with the shell's own\n   `println`, so they arrive on the output medium in order.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.contract :as contract]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def report-primitive\n  \"The primitive name the lowered program calls.\"\n  'py-report)\n\n\n(defn report\n  \"The text of one submission: each `print` call's line, then the uncaught\n   exception as `Type: args`, newline separated. Empty when it did neither.\"\n  [out exception]\n  (str/join\n    \"\\n\"\n    (cond-> (mapv render/line out)\n      exception (conj (str (:type exception)\n                           (when (seq (:args exception))\n                             (str \": \" (str/join \" \"\n                                                 (map render/py-str\n                                                      (:args exception))))))))))\n\n\n(def primitives\n  \"The host primitives the lowered program needs, for a shell's `:primitives`.\"\n  {report-primitive report})\n\n\n(defn display-value\n  \"The text the loop prints for one submission's value: the Python repr,\n   nothing for None.\"\n  [value]\n  (if (or (nil? value) (= :py/None value)) \"\" (render/repr value)))\n\n\n(def ^:private run-form\n  '(let [r (py/run-session %repl-body)\n         text (py-report (get r :py/out) (get r :py/exception))]\n     (if (= text \"\")\n       (get r :py/value)\n       (do (println text) (get r :py/value)))))\n\n\n(defn- ok-packet!\n  [packet]\n  (if (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome packet))\n    packet\n    (throw (ex-info\n             (let [e (first (:yang.cst/errors packet))]\n               (str \"SyntaxError: \" (:message e)\n                    (when (:line e) (str \" (line \" (:line e) \")\"))))\n             {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/syntax\n              :errors (:yang.cst/errors packet)}))))\n\n\n(defn lower-session\n  \"`[ast session']` for one ok CST `packet` under `session` (nil on a fresh\n   session, `:primed` once the prelude has run).\"\n  ([packet session]\n   (lower-session packet session (contract/descriptor contract/legacy-id [])))\n  ([packet session descriptor]\n   (let [packet (ok-packet! packet)\n         packet (cond-> packet\n                  (not (contains? packet :yang.python.antlr/max-digits))\n                  (assoc :yang.python.antlr/max-digits 4300))\n         _ (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"})\n         body (lower/lower-module-body packet nil true descriptor)\n         main (u/let1 '%repl-body\n                      (u/lam [lower/globals-sym lower/globals-fn-sym] body)\n                      (u/sexp->uast run-form))\n         ast (u/mark-tails (if (= :primed session)\n                             main\n                             (u/then prelude/uast main)))]\n     [ast :primed])))\n\n\n(defn lower\n  \"The stateless lowering: a program that carries the prelude.\"\n  [packet]\n  (first (lower-session packet nil)))\n\n\n(defn lower-clojure-session [packet session descriptor]\n  [(lower/lower-packet (ok-packet! packet) {:descriptor descriptor\n                                          :session? true\n                                          :primed? (= :primed session)})\n   :primed])\n\n\n(defn display-clojure-value [value]\n  (if (nil? value) \"\"\n    (if (string? value) (pr-str value) (str value))))\n(ns yin.repl.frontends\n  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure frontend and the ANTLR PHP and\n   Python frontends installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n\n   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n   already read, else the source text.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    #?@(:cljd []\n        :jolt []\n        :default [[yang.php.antlr.cst :as php.antlr.cst]\n                  [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php.antlr.lower]])\n    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-runtime]\n    [yang.python.antlr.contract :as python.contract]\n    [yang.python.antlr.profiles :as python.profiles]\n    [yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.repl]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.parser]\n    [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.probe]\n    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn clojure-manifest\n  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it.\n   Revision c1-2 additionally declares the constructed-collections\n   lowering profile: a dynamically constructed map or set literal now\n   orders its constructor operands by compiled content\n   (:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1), a one-time canonical\n   shift for affected newly compiled artifacts; the C1 support claim,\n   the C1 marker value and the execution grammar versions are\n   unchanged.\"\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-2\"\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  [id {:keys [descriptor-address runtime-address]}]\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision (name id)\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile descriptor-address\n         :yang.frontend/runtime-profile runtime-address\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile descriptor-address\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n\n\n(defn php-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/php :php)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"antlr-p8\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"php\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"htmlDocument\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript}}\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.php/antlr\n         :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :yang.php/antlr\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.php/antlr))\n\n\n(defn- parse-python [source]\n  #?(:jolt\n     (try (python.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))\n          (catch Exception e\n            (if (#{:parser-budget :unavailable-parser} (:diagnostic (ex-data e)))\n              (throw (ex-info (ex-message e) (assoc (ex-data e) :lang :yang/python) e))\n              (throw e))))\n     :default (python.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))))\n\n\n(defn- install-python [catalog id]\n  (let [profile (python.profiles/builtin id)\n        manifest (antlr-manifest id profile)\n        legacy? (= id python.contract/legacy-id)\n        lower (if legacy? python.repl/lower-session python.repl/lower-clojure-session)\n        lower-session (fn [packet session]\n                        (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                        (lower packet session (:descriptor profile)))]\n    (frontend/install catalog manifest\n      (cond-> {:parse (fn [source]\n                         (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                         (parse-python source))\n               :lower (fn [packet] (first (lower-session packet nil)))\n               :lower-session lower-session\n               :derive (fn [packet ast] (python.profiles/derivation manifest profile packet ast))\n               :probe (fn [source]\n                        (python.profiles/verify-builtin! id)\n                        (python.probe/probe source))\n               :render (if legacy? python.repl/display-value python.repl/display-clojure-value)}\n        legacy? (assoc :primitives python.repl/primitives)\n        (not legacy?) (assoc :admit clj-runtime/admit)))))\n\n\n(defn standard\n  \"The standard immutable frontend catalog and the preferred Python revision.\"\n  []\n  (let [catalog (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n                  true (frontend/install (clojure-manifest)\n                                         {:input :forms :parse identity :lower clojure-lower})\n                  #?@(:cljd []\n                      :jolt []\n                      :default [true (frontend/install\n                                       (php-manifest)\n                                       {:parse php.antlr.cst/parse-source\n                                        :lower php.antlr.lower/lower-packet\n                                        :render :php/out})]))]\n    (if #?(:jolt (python.parser/available?) :default true)\n      (-> catalog\n          (install-python python.contract/legacy-id)\n          (install-python python.contract/clojure-id)\n          (assoc :yang.frontend/preferred [:yang/python \"clojure-core-v1\"]))\n      catalog)))\n\n(defn create-state\n  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\n   host supplies its own `:frontends`.  Each binding registers its own\n   `:primitives`; none is merged ambiently.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (repl/create-state (update opts :frontends #(or % (standard))))))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.contract\n  \"The Python grammar's hook ABI and the two versioned entry call shapes.\")\n\n\n(def legacy-id :yang.python/py-v1)\n(def clojure-id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1)\n\n\n;; [exact role, operand count, frozen py export, Clojure-profile export]\n(def ^:private shared-hooks\n  '[[:op/add 2 add add]\n    [:op/sub 2 sub sub]\n    [:op/mul 2 mul mul]\n    [:op/truediv 2 truediv truediv]\n    [:op/floordiv 2 floordiv floordiv]\n    [:op/mod 2 mod mod]\n    [:op/pow 2 pow pow]\n    [:op/neg 1 neg neg]\n    [:op/pos 1 pos pos]\n    [:op/eq 2 eq eq]\n    [:op/ne 2 ne ne]\n    [:op/lt 2 lt lt]\n    [:op/le 2 le le]\n    [:op/gt 2 gt gt]\n    [:op/ge 2 ge ge]\n    [:op/lnot 1 lnot lnot]\n    [:op/truthy 1 truthy truthy]\n    [:coll/vconj 2 vconj vconj]\n    [:coll/list 1 list list]\n    [:coll/tuple 1 tuple tuple]\n    [:coll/set 1 set-from set-from]\n    [:coll/dict 1 dict-from map-from]\n    [:coll/getitem 2 getitem get-item]\n    [:comp/list-new 1 list comp-list-new]\n    [:comp/list-append 2 list-append comp-list-append]\n    [:comp/set-new 0 set-new comp-set-new]\n    [:comp/set-add 2 set-add comp-set-add]\n    [:comp/dict-new 0 dict-new comp-dict-new]\n    [:comp/dict-set 3 dict-set comp-dict-set]\n    [:comp/finish 1 nil comp-finish]\n    [:env/local-get 2 local-get local-get]\n    [:env/global-get 2 global-get global-get]\n    [:env/global-set 3 global-set global-set]\n    [:fn/arg 2 arg arg]\n    [:fn/make 5 make-function make-fn]\n    [:fn/call 2 call call]\n    [:ctrl/for-each 2 for-each for-each]\n    [:ctrl/try 3 try try]\n    [:ctrl/try-finally 2 try-finally try-finally]\n    [:ctrl/raise 1 raise raise]\n    [:ctrl/call-ec 1 call-ec call-ec]])\n\n\n(def ^:private legacy-only\n  ;; The extensions expose the existing shapes of the native runtime. The\n  ;; persistent profile can use its shared hooks or refuse these constructs.\n  '[[as-exception 1]\n    [ascii-conv 1]\n    [assert 2]\n    [bitand 2]\n    [bitor 2]\n    [bitxor 2]\n    [call-kw 3 :calls/kwargs]\n    [class-ns-del 2 :mutation/delete]\n    [class-ns-get 3 :oo/classes]\n    [delattr 2 :mutation/delete]\n    [delattr-quiet 2]\n    [exc-matches 2 :control/except-typed]\n    [extend 2]\n    [format 2]\n    [getattr 2]\n    [global-del 2 :mutation/delete]\n    [global-del-quiet 2]\n    [global-or 3]\n    [iadd 2]\n    [import 2 :modules/import]\n    [import-fail 1 :modules/import]\n    [import-from 2 :modules/import]\n    [import-module? 1 :modules/import]\n    [import-star 2 :modules/import]\n    [import-sub 4 :modules/import]\n    [imul 2]\n    [in 2]\n    [invert 1]\n    [is 2]\n    [is-not 2]\n    [iter 1 :control/generators]\n    [iter-at 2]\n    [iterable 1]\n    [kw-extend 2 :calls/kwstar]\n    [lshift 2]\n    [make-class 2 :oo/classes]\n    [make-exc 2]\n    [make-generator 2 :control/generators]\n    [not-in 2]\n    [object-class 0 :oo/classes]\n    [result! 1]\n    [rshift 2]\n    [setattr 3 :mutation/attribute]\n    [setitem 3 :mutation/subscript]\n    [slice 3]\n    [str 1]\n    [str-conv 2]\n    [unpack 2 :destructuring/unpack]\n    [unpack-star 3 :destructuring/unpack]\n    [with 2 :control/with]\n    [yield 2 :control/generators]\n    [yield-from 2 :control/generators]])\n\n\n(def ^:private shared-requirements\n  {:env/local-get [:mutation/locals]\n   :fn/arg [:calls/positional]\n   :fn/make [:calls/positional]\n   :fn/call [:calls/positional]\n   :comp/list-new [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :comp/list-append [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :comp/set-new [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :comp/set-add [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :comp/dict-new [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :comp/dict-set [:expr/comprehensions]\n   :ctrl/try [:control/exceptions]\n   :ctrl/try-finally [:control/exceptions]\n   :ctrl/raise [:control/exceptions]})\n\n\n(def hook-abi\n  (into {:unit/run-main {:arity 2 :required-by []}}\n        (concat (map (fn [[role arity]]\n                       [role {:arity arity :required-by (get shared-requirements role [])}])\n                     shared-hooks)\n                (map (fn [[export arity capability]]\n                       [(keyword \"legacy\" (name export))\n                        {:arity arity :required-by (if capability [capability] [])}])\n                     legacy-only))))\n\n\n(def entry-lowering\n  {legacy-id {:hook :unit/run-main :arity 1 :params '[body]\n              :call-shapes #{1} :operands [:body-fn]}\n   clojure-id {:hook :unit/run-main :arity 2 :params '[body-fn ambient-resolver]\n               :call-shapes #{2} :operands [:body-fn :ambient-resolver]}})\n\n\n(def legacy-hooks\n  (into {:unit/run-main 'py/run-main :comp/finish nil}\n        (concat (keep (fn [[role _ export]]\n                        (when export [role (symbol \"py\" (name export))])) shared-hooks)\n                (map (fn [[export]]\n                       [(keyword \"legacy\" (name export)) (symbol \"py\" (name export))])\n                     legacy-only))))\n\n\n(def clojure-hooks\n  (into {:unit/run-main 'clj.py/run-main}\n        (map (fn [[role _ _ export]] [role (symbol \"clj.py\" (name export))]))\n        shared-hooks))\n\n\n(def clojure-capabilities\n  {:mutation/locals :cell\n   :mutation/subscript :refused\n   :mutation/attribute :refused\n   :mutation/delete :refused\n   :scope/global :supported\n   :scope/nonlocal :supported\n   :calls/positional :supported\n   :calls/varargs :supported\n   :calls/defaults :refused\n   :calls/kwonly :refused\n   :calls/kwstar :refused\n   :calls/kwargs :refused\n   :destructuring/unpack :refused\n   :expr/comprehensions :supported\n   :control/exceptions :supported\n   :control/except-typed :refused\n   :control/generators :refused\n   :control/with :refused\n   :oo/classes :refused\n   :modules/import :ambient-only})\n\n\n(def