{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '50,110p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc && rg -n 'defn .*invoke-callable|\\\\[clj/invoke-callable|\\\\[clj/raise|defn- read-name|globals-sym|projection-value' src/cljc/yang/{clojure/prelude,python/antlr/lower}.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(defn- fail\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info message data)))\n\n\n(defn bind-params\n  \"Zips params with args, nil-filling any params beyond args' length.\n   Extra args beyond params' length are dropped. §7.7.2: an under-arity\n   call leaves missing parameter names bound to nil, not absent.\"\n  [params args]\n  (into {} (map vector params (concat args (repeat nil)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Application refusals (D6)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; One vocabulary, in the `:reason` shape, for every kernel:\n;;\n;;   :not-applicable      the operator is neither a host function, a\n;;                        closure nor a continuation; carries a coarse\n;;                        `:kind`, never the value\n;;   :foreign-value       a closure or continuation another task minted;\n;;                        carries `:kind :closure` or `:continuation`\n;;   :foreign-format      a continuation of another kernel format or image\n;;   :continuation-arity  a continuation applied to other than one argument\n\n(defn operator-kind\n  \"Classify the operator `f` a kernel of `state` is about to apply:\n   `:host-fn`, `:closure` or `:continuation`. A closure or continuation\n   must be owned by this task (`:owner`); anything else is refused. The\n   one classifier every kernel's application calls.\"\n  [state f]\n  (cond (fn? f) :host-fn\n        (values/host-typed? f)\n        (if (values/owned-by? f (:owner state))\n          (if (values/closure? f) :closure :continuation)\n          (fail \"Cannot apply a value of another task\"\n                {:reason :foreign-value, :kind (values/kind-of f)}))\n        :else (fail \"Cannot apply non-function\"\n                    {:reason :not-applicable, :kind (values/kind-of f)})))\n\n\n(defn marker-mismatch!\n  \"Refuse to lower closure `marker` whose binders (a named kernel's\n   `:yin.k/params`, a positional kernel's `:yin.k/arity`) are not those of\n   the attached lambda it names: a lower mints an applicable closure, so\n   the wire never chooses what a closure binds.\"\n  [marker]\n  (fail \"Closure marker disagrees with its attached lambda\"\n        {:reason :marker-mismatch, :segment (:yin.k/segment marker)}))\n\n\n(defn continuation-argument\n  \"The one value a captured continuation is applied to. Applying a\n   continuation is abortive: the current continuation is discarded and\n   the argument becomes the value of the capture point. Every VM refuses\n   any other arity with this same message.\"\n  [args]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:48:    [clj/raise\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:134:    [clj/invoke-callable\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:812:(def globals-sym\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:837:    (hook-app ctx :legacy/global-or (u/v globals-sym) (global-key ctx name) (u/v globals-fn-sym))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:838:    (hook-app ctx :env/global-get (u/v globals-sym) (global-key ctx name))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:841:(defn- read-name\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:868:      :global (hook-app ctx :env/global-set (u/v globals-sym) (global-key ctx name) value))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:879:      :global (hook-app ctx :legacy/global-del-quiet (u/v globals-sym) (global-key ctx name)))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:896:      :global (hook-app ctx :legacy/global-del (u/v globals-sym) (global-key ctx name)))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1180:(defn- projection-value [{:keys [module export kind] :or {kind :cell-accessor}}]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1207:              (app* 'assoc m (u/lit alias) (projection-value projection)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1280:                                 (projection-value projection))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1289:              (hook-app ctx :legacy/import-star m (u/v globals-sym))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2657:                                (app* 'assoc (u/lit {}) (u/lit :value) (projection-value projection))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2674:                    :body-fn (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym] body)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2775:        body (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2914:                  (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -38 /tmp/dw-p3prime-repl-baseline.log && rg -n 'java|aliases|:test' deps.edn | tail -22 && sed -n '1,110p' docs/agents/roles/compiler-engineer.md\"","aggregated_output":"DEPRECATED: Libs must be qualified, change codox => codox/codox (/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/deps.edn)\nDEPRECATED: Libs must be qualified, change codox => codox/codox (/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/deps.edn)\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n\nFAIL in (probe-buffers-across-lines-test) (python_antlr_test.cljc:449)\nan open bracket\nexpected: (= [\"\" \"(1, 2)\\n\"] (texts (session :yang/python) [\"print((1,\" \"2))\"]))\n  actual: (not (= [\"\" \"(1, 2)\\n\"] [\"\" \"Error: Cannot apply non-function\"]))\n25: :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n31:           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n74:           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n149:;; clj -M:test\n150:;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n151:;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n152:;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n153:;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n154:;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n---\ndescription: Yang Compiler & Universal AST Engineer role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Yang Compiler & Universal AST Engineer\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Source-language parsing and lowering into Universal AST datoms\n- Universal AST schemas, canonicalization, hashing, and round trips\n- Multi-language and multi-target interoperability\n- Compile-time macro expansion, hygiene, and VM boundary coordination\n- Source locations, diagnostics, and deterministic compiler behavior\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Syntax Independence**: Maintain the core principle that syntax is merely a superficial projection of underlying Universal AST datoms.\n2. **Deterministic Lowering**: Ensure that source code lowers unambiguously to structured datoms with canonical content hashes.\n3. **Multi-Target Interoperability**: Support lowering from Clojure, Python, and other dialects into the shared Yin.VM instruction set.\n4. **Macro Hygiene & Stigmergy**: Implement macro transformation pipelines that preserve source location metadata and lexically scoped bindings.\n\n## Implementation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Yang Compiler and Universal AST Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nImplement <task> in <repository-root>. Read <governing-design-file>,\n<source-files>, and <test-files> first. Acceptance criteria:\n- <criterion-1>\n- <criterion-2>\n- <criterion-3>\n\nWork only in named files. If a required dependency demands expansion, stop and\nrequest authorization before editing it. Preserve unrelated changes, do not\nweaken tests, and preserve syntax independence and deterministic lowering. Run\nfocused tests and lint, and inspect the final diff.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nReport changed files, exact test/check outcomes, unresolved concerns, and any\nincomplete work. Do not claim edits or tests that did not occur.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
