{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'range|print|ambient|uncaught' src/cljc/yang/clojure/{core_module,prelude}.cljc docs/design/yang.preludes.md | head -110 && rg -n 'defn-.*lang|:frontend-session|:last-error|:render|:lang' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/yang.preludes.md:62:1. **Everything is a Stream:** Prelude selection, composition, and lowering are pure functions of explicit data configurations and CST streams. External I/O and host capabilities remain declared VM/stream effects (`stream/*`, `cell/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004; prelude composition adds no ambient I/O.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:79:- **\"One truth, many perspectives\" is a stream operation.** The same Python CST packet is one truth; `py-v1` and `clojure-core-v1` are two perspectives. Selecting between them — the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing inversion — is a *re-pin of stream-resident artifacts* (the descriptor and profile addresses), never a callback into the lowerer and never ambient prelude state.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:80:- **The \"explicit local functions\" clause is where the ambient resolver lives:** the `:kind :cell-accessor` projections resolve through the unit-bound `ambient-resolver` passed as data (`[body-fn ambient-resolver]`) — a task-local cell of cells, explicit, named in the provenance, and validated against verified UAST before use.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:97:   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Transitive `:yin.module/footprint` unions are governed by `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:98:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:175:   - Operates exclusively on **boxed `data/float64`** inputs and outputs (plus exact integers where specified), returning either a boxed `data/float64`, a boolean/integer/string, or a pure status keyword (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:180:     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:235:- **`yin.vm.integer` v4 refusal algebra (`src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:81–100`):** Returns keyword reasons for `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:yin.vm.integer/digit-limit`, and `:yin.vm.integer/float-overflow`; every other refusal (`:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range`, `:syntax`, `:zero-division`, `:negative-count`, `:negative-exponent`) throws a host operational failure and **MUST NOT** be caught or relabeled into guest exceptions.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:238:  - Fixed-width wrapping: `wrap-unsigned [x width-pow2 mask]`, `wrap-signed [x half-range range]`, `in-range? [x min-v max-v]` (backing `js/wrap32` and `php/wrap64` / `php/int-result`).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:306:2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:307:3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):** Checks each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive `:yin.module/footprint` through `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:308:4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):** Optional ceiling checked via `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` over the verified `:yin.module/footprint :effects` union.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:323:**Explicit non-goal (avoiding unnecessary N×M complexity):** We do **not** require arbitrary off-diagonal swaps (such as compiling `yang.clojure` syntax onto Python mutable dicts or PHP syntax onto JS prototypes). `yang.clojure` compiles directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` without being forced through a generic hook ABI. Non-Clojure frontends (`yang.python`, `yang.typescript`, `yang.php`) parameterize their lowering through `:yang.semantics/descriptor` to select between their native profile and a Yin/Clojure profile (or custom ambient library projections).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:331:  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), UAST-derived structural export/arity/role verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:345: :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:374:  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:425:  ;; Control flow & unit entry (unit/run-main always takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:433: ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:436: :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:471:2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:** Free source identifiers resolve in strict order: (1) lexical scope (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal`), (2) per-module globals (`:vars` in `globals-cell`), (3) unit-bound ambient resolver (`:ambient` in `globals-cell`, passed via `:unit/run-main`), failing with a guest `NameError` on miss.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:473:   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`, computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**, and inspects every active hook, executable `:literals.*` target, and `:ambient-projections` entry directly against the target manifest's verified `:yin.module/tree` UAST (`wide-app` top-level `(yin/def (quote sym) expr)` definitions):\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:481:6. **Frontend parameterization:** `yang.python.antlr.lower`, `yang.typescript.antlr.lower`, and `yang.php.antlr.lower` read literals, hooks (including 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`, preserving full CPython/Node/PHP oracle and 4-host parity under the legacy pins. **Entry-lowering contracts (r8):** each frontend's contract specifies BOTH entry shapes — the landed native entry shape (`py/run-main` 1-arg, `js` single-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with the request stream in slot two) for the legacy track, and the Clojure profile's resolver-bearing 2-arg `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` shape — so the native mapping is 1:1 against the FROZEN exports and never re-arches them to satisfy the Clojure profile. **Oracle assignment (r8):** native-oracle parity suites gate the LEGACY pins; capability-refusal suites gate the default profile.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:540:| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Checks `(data/contains? (get g :vars) name)` first; on miss invokes unit-owned `((get g :ambient) name)`; presence-vs-payload applies here too (r8) — a projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` returns as-is; only true absence raises the guest `NameError` map built via evaluated `assoc`. |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:541:| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Updates `:vars` in `globals-cell` (preserving `:ambient`) and returns `value`. |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:552:| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, `(clj.py/init!)`; installs `clj.py`'s cold-effect policy handlers (`:math/*`, `:int/*`, `:coll/unsupported-key`) on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; allocates a fresh per-unit `globals` cell; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` and returns the value verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`. |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:573:1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:600:- `is_empty`, `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:618:Verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` (r7: the analyzer's high-degree predicate now counts combined in+out degree ≥ 6, matching this document's rule; `56d17563`). No multi-node cycles and no multi-node SCCs exist. The analyzer prints three SELF-loop warnings (`yang.php.antlr.quoted`, `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` — macro self-reference in defquoted-family namespaces); these are analyzer-reporting artifacts, not runtime dependency cycles, and are expected to disappear once the defquoted consolidation (P0) lands:\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:670:   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against UAST-derived arity/roles, unit-bound `ambient-resolver`, lexical precedence, and reserved-door bans (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`).\n1139:   never changes a live session.  `:lang` selects a frontend by id\n1214:       {:lang lang\n1426:   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\"\n1430:      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:session staged)))))\n1443:   frontend's staged session is committed; a frontend with a `:render`\n1447:        render (:render (::frontend state'))\n2373:(defn- admit-frontend [vm catalog lang]\n2379:(defn- switch-lang\n2386:        (assoc :lang lang :frontend-session nil)\n2412:                         :lang lang\n2419:   (`:frontend-session`, cleared with the VM) and leaves the session it\n2420:   answers, with the binding's `:render`, in the program's\n2425:                        (lower-session parsed (:frontend-session state))\n2428:                 (:render binding) (assoc :render (:render binding))\n2439:  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n2447:  (= :forms (:input (frontend-binding state (:lang state)))))\n2452:  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n2464:  (let [state (assoc state :frontend-session :primed)]\n2469:                            {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n2507:                                                           (:lang state))\n2518:                     (update :vm admit-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))\n2526:          :frontend-session nil\n2613:   its lowering left (`::frontend`: the session and the `:render` hook) is\n2617:   abandoned keeps the shell's previous `:frontend-session`.\"\n2827:  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n2886:  {:lang (:lang state)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
