{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1420,1490p;2360,2440p;2595,2650p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc && sed -n '430,460p;565,607p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\"","aggregated_output":"  [(:shell-token state) (:round state)])\n\n\n(defn- commit-frontend\n  \"Keep what a frontend program's lowering staged (`::frontend`, see\n   `eval-compiled`) now that its VM state survives: the frontend session\n   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [staged (::frontend state)]\n    (cond-> (dissoc state ::frontend)\n      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:session staged)))))\n\n\n(defn- finalize-eval\n  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  Only a\n   result stamped with this round's identity is this round's value; the\n   evaluator answers once per halted program, after its prints.  The\n   render hook and the default result formatting are host code\n   executing at the round's very end; a raise from either reaches the\n   round recovery, which reads retention evidence only from the\n   shell-owned accumulator, never from the raise payload (r11).  A missing\n   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\n   runner recorded.  The program halted, so its VM state survives and a\n   frontend's staged session is committed; a frontend with a `:render`\n   shows its value as that renders it, the loop printing for every language.\"\n  [state state' vm']\n  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n        render (:render (::frontend state'))\n        [state'' output-text results]\n        (drain-output (commit-frontend\n                        (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append))))\n        round (round-id state')\n        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n    (if (seq current)\n      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n         (str output-text\n              (if render\n                (render value)\n                (format-value value (host-fn-namer (:vm state'')))))])\n      [state''\n       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n\n\n(defn- drain-observer\n  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n   stays nil.\"\n  [observer]\n  (when observer\n    (loop [observer observer]\n      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n\n\n(defn- ingress-gaps\n  \"Gaps the evaluation path's observers counted.  The code indexer's are\n   its own: an index loss is reported without refusing evaluation.\"\n  [state]\n  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)))\n\n\n(defn- consume-failed-round\n  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n\n   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n   observers resumes from the session the throw carried — the failing\n    (qualified-keyword? lang) (frontend/select catalog\n                                               {:yang.frontend/id lang})\n    :else (frontend/refused :yang.frontend/unknown {:id lang})))\n\n\n(defn- selected-primitives\n  \"The `:primitives` the binding selected by `lang` registers, else {}.\n   A language's primitives belong to its binding; the primitives of\n   unselected languages are never merged into the session.\"\n  [catalog lang]\n  (or (:primitives (:binding (select-frontend catalog lang))) {}))\n\n\n(defn- admit-frontend [vm catalog lang]\n  (if-let [admit (:admit (:binding (select-frontend catalog lang)))]\n    (update vm :modules admit)\n    vm))\n\n\n(defn- switch-lang\n  \"Select `lang`: its binding's primitives replace the previous binding's\n   in the live VM (host `:extra-primitives` stay over them), and the\n   frontend session is dropped.\"\n  [state lang]\n  (let [new (selected-primitives (:frontends state) lang)]\n    (-> state\n        (assoc :lang lang :frontend-session nil)\n        (update :vm admit-frontend (:frontends state) lang)\n        (assoc-in [:vm :primitives]\n                  (merge (make-repl-primitives (:output-stream state))\n                         new\n                         (:extra-primitives state))))))\n\n\n(defn- usable-binding\n  \"The binding of a successful `selected`, when it has a parse and a lower\n   stage, else nil.\"\n  [selected]\n  (let [binding (when (frontend/ok? selected) (:binding selected))]\n    (when (and (map? binding) (fn? (:parse binding)) (fn? (:lower binding)))\n      binding)))\n\n\n(defn- frontend-binding\n  \"The installed binding for `lang` in the session's pinned catalog.  With\n   no parse and lower stage installed it throws an `unavailable-parser`\n   diagnostic: there is no fallback to another frontend.\"\n  [state lang]\n  (let [selected (select-frontend (:frontends state) lang)]\n    (or (usable-binding selected)\n        (throw (ex-info (str \"unavailable-parser: no parser for \" (pr-str lang))\n                        {:diagnostic :unavailable-parser\n                         :lang lang\n                         :selection selected})))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-parsed\n  \"Lower `parsed` through `binding`.  A binding with a `:lower-session`\n   stage lowers against the frontend session the shell keeps\n   (`:frontend-session`, cleared with the VM) and leaves the session it\n   answers, with the binding's `:render`, in the program's\n   `::frontend` metadata, for `eval-compiled` to stage.\"\n  [state binding parsed]\n  (let [lower-session (:lower-session binding)\n        [ast session] (if lower-session\n                        (lower-session parsed (:frontend-session state))\n                        [((:lower binding) parsed) nil])\n        staged (cond-> {}\n                 (:render binding) (assoc :render (:render binding))\n                 lower-session (assoc :session session)\n                 (:derive binding) (assoc :derivation ((:derive binding) parsed ast)))]\n    (cond-> ast\n      (seq staged) (vary-meta assoc ::frontend staged))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-input\n  \"Lower `input` through the selected frontend; `forms` are the shell\n   reader's forms, used by a frontend that consumes them.\"\n  [state input forms]\n  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n    (lower-parsed state binding\n      trusted [state (str \"Own: \" (pr-str (first (:own (:link-source state))))\n                          \"\\nTrusted: \"\n                          (pr-str (vec (sort (:trusted (:admission state))))))]\n      reset [(rebuild-session\n               (configure-admission state (:initial-admission state))\n               (:vm-type state))\n             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n      help [state help-text]\n      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n      host [state host-text]\n      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n\n\n(defn- eval-compiled\n  \"Evaluate a program `compile-input` or `compile-source` lowered.  What\n   its lowering left (`::frontend`: the session and the `:render` hook) is\n   staged on the round and committed only where the round's VM state\n   survives: when the program halts, now or when its parked require\n   completes (`finalize-eval`).  A round that fails, rolls back, or is\n   abandoned keeps the shell's previous `:frontend-session`.\"\n  [state ast]\n  (let [staged (::frontend (meta ast))\n        [state' text] (eval-program (cond-> state\n                                      staged (assoc ::frontend staged))\n                                    ast)\n        admitted? (and (:derivation staged) (not= (:round state) (:round state')))]\n    [(cond-> (dissoc state' ::frontend)\n       admitted? (assoc-in [:frontend-derivations (round-id state')] (:derivation staged)))\n     text]))\n\n\n(defn- eval-parsed*\n  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n   re-check.\"\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (try\n    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n      (cond\n        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n        forms (eval-compiled state (compile-input state trimmed forms))\n        (forms-input? state) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n        :else (eval-compiled state (compile-source state trimmed))))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n        [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))))\n\n\n(defn- fold-queued\n  \"Evaluate the lines retained while a require was pending, in the order\n   they were typed, each exactly once, and join their texts.  A line that\n  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n\n ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\n ;; `(m/e)`, returning the module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional\n ;; :kind :value references a non-lambda immutable export directly.\n :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in, :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  - *Step C:* Outside `try-value`, reject unsupported `:yang.call/binding-profile` via evaluated `assoc` evidence and transfer `:yang.call/unsupported-binding`.\n  - *Step D:* Run argument binding + body inside **`yrt.effect/try-value`** on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. Normal exit restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the value verbatim; escape inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)` to forward retained protocol conditions without double-wrapping or wrap user escapes via `(yang.call/thrown e)`.\n- **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):** Checks `clj/admitted-callable?` (minting retained `:yang.call/not-callable` on failure), else calls `yang.call/invoke` with a `raise-exit` that unwraps `:yang.call/thrown` and retains all other protocol conditions via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance`.\n\n### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n\nIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n\n1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n   - **Cell-safe collection predicates:** `impl-cell-ref?` ensures authenticated callable cells answer **`false`** to all of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`; `impl-fn?` matches `clj/admitted-callable?` 1-to-1.\n   - **Host-backed portable operations (zero guest-UAST leak workarounds):**\n     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`, `impl-rem`, `impl-int?`: delegate to `integer/*` + `yrt.int/check-limit` and `float/add`/`float/sub`.\n     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n     - `impl-str`: deterministic renderer delegating ints to `integer/format`, floats to `float/format`, keywords/symbols to `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`, maps/sets to `data/canonical-entries`, and authenticated cells to `\"#<fn>\"`.\n     - `impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-vec`, `impl-keys`, `impl-vals`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-into`, `impl-merge`, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`: normalize maps/sets via `data/canonical-entries`.\n     - Map/set mutators and lookups (`impl-assoc`, `impl-get`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj`, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into`, etc.): enforce `data/admit-key?`.\n     - Explicitly excluded: `var?`, `resolve`, `invoke-value`.\n2. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   - Requires `clj` and `clojure.core.impl`. Exports only cell-free pure functions at install time: idempotent 0-arg `init!` (building `{sym cell}` with `clj/prim-assoc` and `clj/make-callable`), 1-arg `export` (using `clj/prim-get`), and 0-arg cell-accessor exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`.\n   - Dynamic closures (`impl-comp`, `impl-partial`) construct cells via `clj/make-callable`; all dynamic callbacks (`map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `update`, etc.) invoke via `clj/invoke-callable`.\n   - **Direct `yang.clojure` migration in P3:** Retires `yang.clojure`'s inline `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path so there is one unified Clojure runtime.\n\n### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n\n```python\ndef sum_even_squares(xs):\n    if is_empty(xs):\n        return 0\n    evens = filter(lambda n: n % 2 == 0, xs)\n    squares = map(lambda n: n * n, evens)\n    return reduce(lambda a, b: a + b, 0, squares)\n```\n\n- `is_empty`, `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (backed by `:pure` `yin.vm.integer` / `yin.vm.float` / `data/equiv`).\n- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), returned verbatim.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
