{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"The descriptor’s ambient table omits `range` and `print`, so the native fixtures that call them need the `py-v1` pin. I also found why the default REPL says “Cannot apply non-function” when name lookup fails: an uncaught guest error reaches the runtime’s unhandled fallback. I’ll fix that at the REPL boundary and verify the comprehension with a vector input the default profile supports."}}
