{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def.*app\\\\*|def.*v |def.*then|def.*if-node|def.*let1' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/uast.cljc && sed -n '15,65p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc && sed -n '1125,1155p;2455,2475p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc && rg -n 'status|ERROR' /tmp/dw-p3prime-repl-compare.log\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/uast.cljc:11:(def v core/v)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/uast.cljc:20:(def if-node core/if-node)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/uast.cljc:32:(def then core/then)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/uast.cljc:38:(def let1 core/let1)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:236:(def ^:private app* core/app*)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2095:  \"`@d1 ... @dn def f` (or `class`): the def's own lowering, then the\n\n   Decided lowering rules (collab/1790795118566 brief):\n   - Every function-local binding and every parameter is a cell, allocated\n     at function entry: parameters initialised, other locals `:py/unbound`.\n     Reads are `py/local-get` (unbound -> UnboundLocalError), writes\n     `cell/set!`. Module names and `global` names live in the module's\n     namespace dict, `%globals` (`py/global-get`, a miss is NameError;\n     `py/global-set`); `yin/def` appears only in the prelude; builtins\n     are read through the task's builtins dict.\n   - A `def` or `lambda` is a function object (`py/make-function`) whose\n     code takes one argument vector; every call is `(py/call f [args])` or,\n     with keywords, `(py/call-kw f [args] [[name value] ...])`; the callee\n     binds positional, keyword, default, `*args` and `**kwargs`.\n   - Control flow is continuations: a function with a `return` runs its body\n     under `py/call-ec`; loops are self-applied lambdas whose `break` and\n     `continue` are escapes; `try` installs a handler continuation through\n     `py/try`, and `raise` invokes the innermost one. `finally` is a\n     `py/try-finally` frame that every exit runs; `with` is `py/with`, the\n     language reference's expansion over the same two forms.\n   - Tuple, list and starred targets unpack with `py/unpack` /\n     `py/unpack-star`; comprehensions run in their own scope with the first\n     iterable evaluated outside it. List, set and dict comprehensions are\n     eager; a generator expression is an anonymous generator whose first\n     iterable is evaluated and `iter()`-checked at creation, every other\n     clause lazily, at each resume.\n   - `import m` (C4 I1) lowers at the statement to `(py/import m\n     pym.m/spec pym.m/body)` plus the binding of the module object, one\n     `(require 'pym.m)` hoisted per import in the program wrapper (linked\n     only); `sys` and `builtins` come pre-seeded with no delivery. `del\n     m.y` is a delattr call, `del x` an unbind. I2: `import a.b.c` loads\n     the chain `a`, `a.b` (`pym.a$b`), `a.b.c` in order through\n     `py/import-sub`, which sets each fresh submodule on its parent;\n     `as`, `from` (`py/import-from`), `*` (`py/import-star`) and relative\n     imports, resolved statically against the unit's declared name and\n     package-ness, a failure raising at the statement (`py/import-fail`).\n   - A function whose body yields is a generator function: its code binds\n     the arguments and allocates the cells, then returns\n     `(py/make-generator name (fn [%gen] body))`; each `yield v` is\n     `(py/yield %gen v)`, each `yield from x` `(py/yield-from %gen x)`.\n     The `:gen` binder is reset in every nested scope,\n     so a `yield` at module or class level, or in a comprehension's or\n     generator expression's own scope, is a syntax error.\n   - Operators, truthiness, equality, objects and exceptions are prelude\n     calls (`yang.python.antlr.prelude`).\n\n   Generated names come from CST node ids (`%brk17`, `%w17`, ...): unique per\n   node, deterministic, and `%` cannot begin a Python identifier. Guest\n   locals keep their Python names in the lexical env. Generated hook\n   calls use their qualified exports and cannot be captured by a local.\n   An implicit class base reads the native hook, bypassing runtime keys.\"\n  (:require\n\n   `:custody` is an optional custody composition value\n   (yin.vm.ucf.compose): the shell only carries it, as data, so the\n   host's single step owner can advance it (yin.repl.main/step-all --\n   the custody control step runs during hydration and through the\n   bounded shutdown drain; the custody program step runs only while\n   the shell is admitted and running).  Nothing in the shell reads or\n   steps it; nil, the default, is today's behaviour.\n\n   `:frontends` is the frontend catalog (`yang.frontend`) the session\n   compiles through, composed by the host entry point (this namespace\n   requires no frontend; see `yin.repl.frontends`).  Without it the catalog\n   is empty and every compile answers `unavailable-parser`.  The session\n   pins this immutable snapshot: installing into another catalog value\n   never changes a live session.  `:lang` selects a frontend by id\n   (`:yang/python`) or by `[id revision]`; a language keyword is not a\n   selector. The default is the `:yang/clojure` frontend.\n   one the catalog cannot answer is an `unavailable-parser` diagnostic,\n   never a fallback to another frontend.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n            content-store content-client name-env link-policy index-store\n            index-store-spec link-source recovery principals follow custody\n            frontends admission publication-policy publication-media\n            host-modules publisher-key]\n     :or {lang :yang/clojure vm-type :semantic admission {}}}]\n   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n         shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n         index-store-spec (cond\n                            (and index-store index-store-spec)\n                   (if (= :forms (:input binding)) (read-forms input) input)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-command-ast\n  \"The AST `(compile ...)` previews.  It lowers against a primed frontend\n   session: a session-staged frontend carries its prelude only on the\n   session's first lowering, and the preview is of the submitted form, not\n   of the runtime it would run on.  The session itself is not touched.\"\n  [state arg]\n  (let [state (assoc state :frontend-session :primed)]\n    (cond\n      (string? arg) (compile-source state arg)\n      (forms-input? state) (compile-input state nil [arg])\n      :else (throw (ex-info \"This compile command expects a source string\"\n                            {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n\n\n(defn- render-compile-output\n  \"Render the frontend syntax, the input row batch, and what the session's\n   expander would make of it against its current store: the expanded tree\n   packet (or the expansion error) and the event rows.  The expansion is a\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
